id: pm-5rexki
title: "Extension-registered item types are created, stored and versioned like any other item but are invisible to the merge fence and its drift detector, which reports the fence clean"
description: "An item of an extension-contributed type is written to an unfenced folder, so concurrent branch edits fall back to git line-based merge on a TOON document while merge install reports changed:false."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: customization,data-durability,extensions,merge-safety,multi-agent,pm-cli
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:03:14.126Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:29.627Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "An item of an extension-registered type is covered by the field-aware TOON/markdown merge driver in a clean clone after pm merge install; The committed fence remains a deterministic function of persisted project state, so local default validation never recommends a change the CI gate reverts (pm-mkzw1x property preserved); Where coverage is genuinely absent, health or validate names the unfenced folder and the extension that registered its type, instead of reporting clean; A merge conformance test drives two branches editing different fields of one extension-typed item and asserts no field is lost"
value: Restores the field-aware merge guarantee for the exact item population a universal tracker is supposed to serve.
impact: "Silent field loss on concurrent branch merges of custom-typed items, with no warning surface."
why_now: "Universal customization and multi-agent merge safety are both flagship claims; today using either one silently disables the other, and the detector reports success."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "HEAD 2026.7.30, clean sandbox git repo, pm-digital-twin installed --project; also reproduced against this repository workspace"
repro_steps: git init && pm init; pm install packages/pm-digital-twin --project; pm create --title X --type TwinAsset; pm merge install --dry-run | grep -c twin  =>  0
expected_result: "Any folder that can hold an item document is covered by the field-aware merge driver, or a diagnostic names it as unprotected."
actual_result: "twin-assets/, twin-facilities/, cards/, changesets/, refs/ hold item documents with no merge attribute; merge install --dry-run reports changed:false and no diagnostic mentions them."
component: sdk/merge
